    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0562" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg456"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese consul-general
                        to Mr. Tsui</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Two Chinese merchants and one student holding certificates issued by Chinese
                    consul at Yokohama properly viséed by American consul arrived per steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of Pekin</hi>. Collector refuses to land them,
                    mainly on the ground that Chinese consuls have no right to issue certificate or
                    passport to Chinese merchants or exempt class residing at their ports to come to
                    the United States. See Department on the matter immediately. Steamer departs
                    June 2.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Li Yung Yew</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chinese Consul-General</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
